1. and 2. It is not considered to be in the public interest to divulge war establishments of military units, nor is it departmental policy to release individual unit strengths. However, as of July 1, 1968, there were Infantry battalions, viz:	1 RCR; 2 RCR;
1	PPCLI; 2 PPCLI; 1 RHC; 2 RHC; 1 CDNGds;
2	CDNGds; 1 R22eR; 2 R22eR; 3 R22eR; 1 QOR of C; 2 QOR of C; with a total strength of 8,557.
3.	None has been disbanded but 2 QOR of C was reduced to nil strength effective August 15, 1968 and 1 CDNGds will be reduced to nil strength effective October 1, 1968.

1. and 2. It is not considered to be in the public interest to divulge war establishments of military units, nor is it departmental policy to release individual unit strengths. However, as of July 1, 1968, there were four engineer squadrons, viz: 1 Fd Sqn; 2 Fd Sqn;
3	Fd Sqn; 4 Fd Sqn; with a total strength of 1173.
3.	No.

Resolved, that a sum not exceeding $3,776,197,303.75 being the aggregate of-
(a)	nine-twelfths of the total of all items set forth in the revised main estimates, 1968-69, for the fiscal year ending the 31st of March, 1969, laid before the House of Commons at the present session of parliament, $4,852,052,274.75;
(b)	an additional two-twelfths of Energy, Mines and Resources item 60, Finance item 30, Legislation item 15, Public Works items 25 and 30, Secretary of State item 2, Transport items 15, 25 and 90, Treasury Board item 25, Loans, Investments and Advances items L35 and L125, (Schedule A) of the said revised main estimates, $35,666,415,67;
(c)	an additional one-twelfth of Agriculture item 15, Energy, Mines and Resources item 75, Indian Affairs and Northern Development item 34, National Defence items 20 and 50, Privy Council item 15, Regional Development item 25, Secretary of
September 30, 1968

State items 1 and 65, Transport item 5, (Schedule B) of the said revised main estimates, $6,681,409.50;
Less the amounts authorized by Appropriation Act No. 2, 1968, $1,118,202,797.17,
be granted to Her Majesty on account of the fiscal year ending the 31st of March, 1969.
